# CODEOWNERS — who must review a change to the paths that decide what the site publishes.
#
# INERT SINCE 11 NOV 2026: the author removed "Require review from Code Owners" from the ruleset on `main`
# (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §3a, rows 2 and 3), so nothing here requires a review. The file is kept, because turning
# the requirement back on makes it work again. What follows is what it did while the requirement was on.
#
# This file does nothing by itself. It takes effect only together with a branch ruleset on `main`
# that turns on "Require review from Code Owners" (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §3a, rows 2 and 3). With a
# single administrator GitHub will not let that person approve their own pull request, so the
# ruleset needs either a second reviewer or the owner on its bypass list; the release gate cannot
# know which was chosen.
#
# One owner per path. The paths are the ones docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §3a row 3 names: the workflows
# (the gate is in pages.yml), the release dispatcher and gate, the decision ledger and reviewer
# registry, and the allowlist that is the one home of what is published.

/.github/                          @andreatosti2001
/agent/release/                    @andreatosti2001
/agent/implement/decisions/        @andreatosti2001
/tools/pages-artifact.mjs          @andreatosti2001
